9", "journal_title": "Found.Phys."}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "33", "artid": "352", "page_start": "352", "journal_title": "Appl.Opt."}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "75", "artid": "4337", "page_start": "4337", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.Lett."}}, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2730807"}}], "number_of_pages": 6, "referenced_authors_bais": ["B.G.Englert.1", "A.Y.Shih.1", "P.Kwiat.1", "M.O.Scully.1", "W.H.Zurek.1", "A.Zeilinger.1", "T.Nonn.1", "R.Yu.1", "G.Rempe.1", "K.Mattle.1", "H.Walther.3", "H.Weinfurter.1", "T.J.Herzog.1", "W.K.Wootters.1", "S.Durr.3", "Y.H.Kim.8", "S.P.Kulik.1", "R.A.Beth.3", "H.Y.Shih.2", "A.V.Sergienko.1"], "legacy_version": "20190516084308.0", "inspire_categories": [{"term": "General Physics"}, {"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "legacy_creation_date": "2008-09-29", "preprint_date": "2002-03", "author_count": 4, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "7 pages, 9 figures, Submitted to Phys. Rev. A"}], "first_author": {"full_name": "Walborn, S.P.", "last_name": "Walborn", "first_name": "S.P.", "recid": 1953577}, "control_number": 610769, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevA.65.033818"}, {"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevA.65.033818"}], "earliest_date": "2002-03", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Walborn:2002zza"], "abstracts": [{"source": "APS", "value": "We report a quantum eraser experiment which actually uses a Young double slit to create interference. The experiment can be considered an optical analogy of an experiment proposed by Scully, Englert, and Walther [Nature (London) 351, 111 (1991)]. One photon of an entangled pair is incident on a Young double slit of appropriate dimensions to create an interference pattern in a distant detection region. Quarter-wave plates, oriented so that their fast axes are orthogonal, are placed in front of each slit to serve as which-path markers. The quarter-wave plates mark the polarization of the interfering photon and thus destroy the interference pattern. To recover interference, we measure the polarization of the other entangled photon. In addition, we perform the experiment under “delayed erasure” circumstances.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "APS"}}, {"source": "arXiv", "value": "We report a quantum eraser experiment which actually uses a Young double-slit to create interference. The experiment can be considered an optical analogy of an experiment proposed by Scully, Englert and Walther. One photon of an entangled pair is incident on a Young double-slit of appropriate dimensions to create an interference pattern in a distant detection region. Quarter-wave plates, oriented so that their fast axes are orthogonal, are placed in front of each slit to serve as which-path markers. The quarter-wave plates mark the polarization of the interfering photon and thus destroy the interference pattern. To recover interference, we measure the polarization of the other entangled photon. In addition, we perform the experiment under delayed erasure circumstances.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "refereed": true, "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-7985487"}], "titles": [{"title": "Double-slit quantum eraser"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "A double-slit quantum eraser"}], "facet_author_name": ["2139400_S. Pádua", "1953577_Stephen P. Walborn", "2189784_M.O. Terra Cunha", "2189788_C.H. Monken"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:610769", "updated": "2025-10-01T11:08:17.998935"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rev.A", "Phys. Rev. A"], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph"], "value": "quant-ph/0106078"}]}, "created": "2008-09-29T00:00:00+00:00", "id": "610769"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.65.033818&size=5&page=1"